>>
Rule 32 (Integer indices only valid with int-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5
>>
Rule 33 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 34 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 36 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
